            "review_title": "Review at Paulie's Pizza & Pasta",
            "review_text": "BillTuckerUS\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam51 contributions\n0\nExcellent, Just Excellent, Food\nJun 2020\nWe've had some combination of dining and and takeout four times now. Four of us agree is that this is the best pizza crust we've had in Ho Chi Minh City. The plain Margarita with just cheese and tomato sauce is a real treat - reminds me of what I had on the beach in Genoa many decades ago.\n\nThe mixed salad gets applause from all.\n\nThe way the pasta meals work is that you choose your sauce and then you choose the type of pasta that you want with it.\n\nMy favorite so far was spaghetti aglio olio. I'd have it again next time, except I want to try the calzone, so unless I can arrange to share with somebody it'll have to wait.\n\nMy sole complaint is that, so far, they don't have wine. They promise to have it soon. There's something wrong with the universe when I sit down to an Italian meal without a glass of wine at hand.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 5, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
